      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If you're experiencing significant hives, facial swelling, and throat tingling, it's important to take these symptoms seriously. While Benadryl (diphenhydramine) can help with mild reactions, your symptoms might indicate a more severe allergic reaction, such as anaphylaxis, which can become life-threatening. It's still urgent that you consult medical professionals to receive proper treatment. If the symptoms worsen before you can get to the emergency room, use your phone to call emergency services immediately. Don't wait to go to the ER -- your safety is the most important priority.",
